{
  "title": "TelegramGuard: an iLang-driven guardian bot for Telegram groups",
  "description": "<p>A self-hostable Telegram bot that keeps a group clean and answers its members. Moderation, vision and chat behaviour are defined as iLang prompt specifications rather than prose. Version 1.1 adds convergence-only learning: every spam verdict of the language-model judge is distilled into a deduplicated, counted hard library that serves as a zero-cost deterministic fallback judge when the model is unavailable, is self-pruning, and is exported each release as an open spam corpus in iLang form; plus two deterministic join-time rules (name-is-spam rejection and first-message probe removal). Method note with cited literature in docs/METHOD.md. Readme in six languages.</p>",
